WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.300
-We're here with Jennifer Lopez.

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:07.634
Her new movie "Marry Me"
is in theaters February 11th.

00:00:07.634 --> 00:00:11.701
And I should mention that I have
a cameo in this movie.

00:00:11.701 --> 00:00:12.834
-You do have a cameo.

00:00:12.834 --> 00:00:14.534
-We're in a movie together.
-Two cameos.

00:00:14.534 --> 00:00:16.200
-I know. I had two cam--
Pretty important scenes.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:17.501
-Really important scenes.

00:00:17.501 --> 00:00:19.334
Actually, one of the scenes
was really important.

00:00:19.334 --> 00:00:20.601
It was very emotional.

00:00:20.601 --> 00:00:22.167
Because it's one
of those moments

00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:24.200
where, like,
people don't get to see

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:27.701
where I kind of had to, like,
let down my guard, too,

00:00:27.701 --> 00:00:32.100
where she suffers this terrible
kind of public humiliation

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:33.634
and is on her way home.

00:00:33.634 --> 00:00:38.400
And like the night talk show
hosts do, they're roasting her.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:42.467
And she's crying on the floor
in a puddle.

00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:43.601
You know what I mean?

00:00:43.601 --> 00:00:44.767
And it's just, like,
one of those moments

00:00:44.767 --> 00:00:46.534
that people don't
really think about.

00:00:46.534 --> 00:00:48.000
You know, you don't think,
"Oh, God.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.868
Maybe they're laughing at home.
Maybe they can take a joke."

00:00:50.868 --> 00:00:52.300
And sometimes it just --
-It just hurts.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:54.467
-It just hurts.
-It just hurts, yeah.

00:00:54.467 --> 00:00:57.067
And this was the first time,
like, I got to, like, do that.

00:00:57.067 --> 00:00:58.767
Because, you know,
we're in show business.

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:00.367
We like to
put our best foot forward.

00:01:00.367 --> 00:01:03.033
We're out here. You don't need
to know about our nonsense.

00:01:03.033 --> 00:01:05.701
You just sing the song,
do the dance.

00:01:05.701 --> 00:01:07.567
We entertain.
We have a good time.

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:09.167
But there's a human being there,

00:01:09.167 --> 00:01:11.167
and I think this movie
kind of gets into that.

00:01:11.167 --> 00:01:13.801
And you are the talk show host
who's roasting me.

00:01:13.801 --> 00:01:15.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.267 --> 00:01:17.968
-I love that I got permission
to roast your character, yeah.

00:01:17.968 --> 00:01:19.701
But I do think you are perfect
for that

00:01:19.701 --> 00:01:20.834
'cause you get to see
all the stuff.

00:01:20.834 --> 00:01:22.501
And it's such public stuff.

00:01:22.501 --> 00:01:25.067
Everything you do is so public,
'cause you're that famous.

00:01:25.067 --> 00:01:28.067
-Yes.
-So, you're having a concert.

00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:29.934
You have a very public breakup.
-Yeah.

00:01:29.934 --> 00:01:32.801
-And someone, being Owen Wilson,
is in the crowd

00:01:32.801 --> 00:01:34.167
and has a sign up.

00:01:34.167 --> 00:01:35.834
-Who is so good in this movie!

00:01:35.834 --> 00:01:37.467
Oh, my God, you will love him
in this movie.

00:01:37.467 --> 00:01:39.434
-He knows how to do it, right?
He knows how to do it.

00:01:39.434 --> 00:01:40.968
-He just grounds
the whole thing.

00:01:40.968 --> 00:01:42.367
He's just so amazing.

00:01:42.367 --> 00:01:44.701
He just has
so much heart and soul.

00:01:44.701 --> 00:01:46.033
We're so different.

00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:48.133
And we're supposed to be.
We're supposed to be.

00:01:48.133 --> 00:01:49.434
-Opposites attract.
-Yes, yes.

00:01:49.434 --> 00:01:50.868
-Well, basically,
you're just fed up,

00:01:50.868 --> 00:01:54.067
and someone's holding a sign up
at a concert, like you do.

00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:56.200
And his says, "Marry me,"
and you go, "Okay."

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:57.901
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.901 --> 00:02:00.100
-It's like, wait,
what just happened?

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:01.901
-Nothing else is working out.

00:02:01.901 --> 00:02:03.767
How about this?
-"Okay, I'm gonna marry you."

00:02:03.767 --> 00:02:05.234
-Let's do it.
-"You want to get married?

00:02:05.234 --> 00:02:07.033
Let's just do it."
And he's like, "What?"

00:02:07.033 --> 00:02:10.667
-Yeah, and it turns into
a whole frenzy with social media

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:12.834
and everything that happens,
and it gets out.

00:02:12.834 --> 00:02:15.234
-It's a great idea.
-Yeah. It's fun.

00:02:15.234 --> 00:02:16.968
-Do you have any memorable signs

00:02:16.968 --> 00:02:19.567
that you see
when you have your concerts?

00:02:19.567 --> 00:02:20.834
-So many.
-Yeah.

00:02:20.834 --> 00:02:22.767
-So many.
I mean, I think when I first --

00:02:22.767 --> 00:02:24.501
I went on tour pretty late
in my career.

00:02:24.501 --> 00:02:25.934
I didn't go
until I was in my 40s

00:02:25.934 --> 00:02:27.834
and I had kids
and everything like that.

00:02:27.834 --> 00:02:32.534
And so I hadn't tour for like --
I don't know how many.

00:02:32.534 --> 00:02:34.267
12 years I had been
recording music,

00:02:34.267 --> 00:02:36.300
and I had never done
a proper world tour.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.868
I'd done shows, of course,
here and there always.

00:02:38.868 --> 00:02:41.400
But I remember this woman
holding up this sign

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:43.367
and saying, "I've been
waiting 14 years."

00:02:43.367 --> 00:02:46.667
Oh, my God,
it's gonna make me cry.

00:02:46.667 --> 00:02:51.167
She said -- She said,
"I've been waiting for 14 years

00:02:51.167 --> 00:02:55.701
to tell you that you helped me
be the woman that I am today."

00:02:55.701 --> 00:02:57.868
I was like, "Oh, my God."

00:02:57.868 --> 00:03:00.400
-That's cool, right?
That's powerful.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:03.234
Because I had never toured --
It was so sweet.

00:03:03.234 --> 00:03:05.300
It was just like
you don't realize,

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:06.534
like, your music
is touching people.

00:03:06.534 --> 00:03:07.834
You just think you're just
doing this thing.

00:03:07.834 --> 00:03:10.000
We do this thing,
and you don't realize that

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.701
until you, like, tour the world
and people come up to you,

00:03:12.701 --> 00:03:13.968
and I would do
the meet and greets,

00:03:13.968 --> 00:03:16.567
and they would, you know,
tell me, like --

00:03:16.567 --> 00:03:19.767
show me tattoos of my name
on their back.

00:03:19.767 --> 00:03:22.167
And so I'm like,
"What is happening here?"

00:03:22.167 --> 00:03:23.868
And it was just amazing
to see it.

00:03:23.868 --> 00:03:25.567
So that was
a very memorable sign.

00:03:25.567 --> 00:03:27.033
I always think about that.

00:03:27.033 --> 00:03:29.701
-I'm so happy you're here.
Congrats on the film.

00:03:29.701 --> 00:03:32.000
And thanks for performing
tonight with Maluma.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:33.834
-Yes! We perform.
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:03:33.834 --> 00:03:36.167
Here's the clip
from the movie "Marry Me."

00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:38.467
-Okay, now, I'm guessing
from the way you're holding that

00:03:38.467 --> 00:03:40.133
that you haven't done
too much bowling.

00:03:40.133 --> 00:03:41.601
-Uh, what do I do?

00:03:41.601 --> 00:03:44.934
-Well, you're gonna want to put
your fingers in the holes there.

00:03:44.934 --> 00:03:46.334
Yeah, get your thumb
in that one.

00:03:46.334 --> 00:03:49.067
-There, that one?
-Yep. And then take three steps.

00:03:49.067 --> 00:03:50.467
Kind of you want
to land on your left,

00:03:50.467 --> 00:03:52.300
and don't be afraid
to use those little --

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:00.334
-Strike is better than a spare,
right?

00:04:00.334 --> 00:04:02.834
-That is not
your first time bowling.

00:04:02.834 --> 00:04:04.501
-Yes!
Did you get that?

00:04:04.501 --> 00:04:07.434
-Come on!
Little rope-a-dope.

00:04:07.434 --> 00:04:09.200
-Oh, my God,
I wish I put money on this,

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:12.667
because people are loving it.
-What people?

00:04:12.667 --> 00:04:14.234
-Oh, this is
an Instagram Live feed,

00:04:14.234 --> 00:04:18.234
and 237,000 people are like,
"Why is he such a boring nerd?"

00:04:18.234 --> 00:04:20.200
-Mel.
-What? Their words, not mine.

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:22.767
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:22.767 --> 00:04:26.634
It's so well done and modern
and cool and great direction.

00:04:26.634 --> 00:04:29.734
The director is Kat Coiro.
Unbelievable.

00:04:29.734 --> 00:04:31.667
Congrats on this movie.

00:04:31.667 --> 00:04:32.767
You know I love you.
-Thanks.

00:04:32.767 --> 00:04:34.200
-Jennifer Lopez, everybody.

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:37.868
"Marry Me" is in theaters
February 11th

00:04:37.868 --> 00:04:39.133
and streaming on Peacock.

